& [IR4LangGraphProofRuntimeImplementationPlanV1] is the IR4-S05 implementation plan and dependency boundary for future LangGraph proof runtime activation
  + [plan_id] is ir4-langgraph-proof-runtime-implementation-plan-v1
  + [plan_uuid] is e3b0fdf1-24bb-4eb0-903f-6934d98bc058
  + [slice_id] is IR4-S05
  + [plan_status] is accepted_by_completion_review_pending
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [implementation_scope] is implementation file inventory, dependency boundary, generated output boundary, command plan, and proof checklist only

  = must: define future implementation files, public API boundaries, dependency decision boundary, generated checkpoint roots, fixture runner boundaries, command plan, and proof checklist
  = must: preserve that actual code creation and dependency installation remain gated until later implementation activation slices accept them
  = must: keep all future runtime side effects inside accepted generated output roots
  - never: write graph runtime code, install LangGraph, create fixture source, create expected ledgers, create generated checkpoints, create tests, authorize operations control, or authorize live machine control in this slice

& [ImplementationFileInventory: IR4LangGraphProofRuntime] is the future file inventory for bounded IR4 implementation
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/runtime/graph_state.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is define frozen graph state, terminal outcome, node result, checkpoint envelope, and non-authority warning records
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/runtime/graph_contracts.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is define graph node/edge contracts, precondition/postcondition helpers, and terminal outcome classifiers
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/runtime/graph_runner.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is evaluate the accepted WholeFieldPlannerGraph over fixture records without live dispatch or hidden source writes
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/runtime/checkpoints.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is validate checkpoint freshness, build generated checkpoint records, and refuse checkpoint authority confusion
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/runtime/interrupts.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is build SOP-first interrupt context packets and resume-condition classification records
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/runtime/fixture_runner.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is load tracked IR4 fixture source and expected ledgers, run graph fixtures, write generated outputs only under accepted roots, and compare output to expected ledgers
  + [future_code_file] is src/langsop/runtime/__init__.py
  + [future_code_file_role] is expose only bounded proof-runtime APIs and keep live-control names absent
  + [future_test_file] is tests/test_ir4_runtime_graph_contracts.py

  = must: require deeper reasoning review before creating or editing files outside this inventory for IR4 runtime implementation
  = must: keep code and test creation gated until specific implementation activation slices open

& [DependencyBoundary: IR4LangGraphProofRuntime] is the dependency boundary for future IR4 implementation
  + [dependency_policy] is no dependency installation authorized by IR4-S05
  + [first_pass_dependency_set] is Python standard library only unless a later activation slice explicitly authorizes LangGraph installation
  + [future_dependency_candidate] is langgraph
  + [future_dependency_candidate_status] is gated_until_dependency_authorizing_activation_slice
  + [future_dependency_candidate_reason] is executable LangGraph integration should occur only after graph contracts, fixtures, generated-output roots, and no-authority-promotion tests are accepted
  + [external_dependency_set] is empty_for_current_slice

  = must: require a dependency-authorizing slice before adding packages, lockfiles, imports, or runtime requirements
  = must: keep any standard-library graph runner clearly marked as proof-runtime implementation, not a substitute for accepted LangGraph dependency activation if true LangGraph integration is later required

& [PublicAPIBoundary: IR4LangGraphProofRuntime] is the future public API boundary for IR4 implementation
  + [api] is validate_graph_state(state, boundary_index, policy) returns validation result or terminal fault
  + [api] is run_whole_field_planner_graph(graph_request, operator_harness, policy) returns terminal outcome and graph trace
  + [api] is validate_checkpoint(checkpoint, freshness_basis, policy) returns current, stale, or checkpoint_authority_confusion
  + [api] is build_interrupt_context(interrupt_kind, graph_state, evidence_refs, policy) returns SOP-first interrupt packet
  + [api] is validate_generated_runtime_path(path, generated_output_policy) returns accepted generated path or refusal
  + [api] is run_runtime_graph_fixture(fixture_case, expected_ledger, runner_policy) returns generated fixture comparison report
  + [api_status] is future implementation target only

  = must: make refusal, stale, fault, interrupt, and non-authority status visible in return values
  = must: avoid APIs named or shaped as live dispatch, job control, process control, GPU control, network control, credential access, operations control, or live machine control

