& [ImplementationCommandPlan: IR4LangGraphProofRuntime] is the future command and verification plan
  + [baseline_test_command] is python -m unittest discover -s tests
  + [baseline_compile_command] is python -m compileall -q src tests
  + [future_targeted_test] is python -m unittest tests.test_ir4_runtime_graph_contracts
  + [diff_hygiene_command] is git diff --check
  + [generated_output_review] is prove generated checkpoints, traces, and reports are ignored, disposable, and reproducible

  = must: run baseline tests and diff hygiene after every future implementation slice
  = must: run targeted runtime graph tests once tests.test_ir4_runtime_graph_contracts exists

& [ImplementationProofChecklist: IR4LangGraphProofRuntime] is the proof checklist for later implementation activation
  + [proof_check] is implementation files match ImplementationFileInventory: IR4LangGraphProofRuntime
  + [proof_check] is external dependency set remains empty unless a dependency-authorizing activation slice accepts LangGraph or another dependency
  + [proof_check] is graph state validation rejects missing authority, stale checkpoint, unsupported scope, hidden write, and checkpoint authority confusion
  + [proof_check] is graph runner returns terminal blocked, stale, fault, or interrupt records instead of silent success for unsafe states
  + [proof_check] is operator harness calls remain in-process and bounded to accepted contracts
  + [proof_check] is generated checkpoint, trace, and report writers refuse paths outside accepted generated roots
  + [proof_check] is fixture runner reads only tracked fixture source and expected ledgers and writes only generated outputs
  + [proof_check] is generated checkpoints, traces, and reports are ignored, disposable, and reproducible
  + [proof_check] is source files, expected ledgers, and tracked SOP authority are not mutated by runtime code or tests
  + [proof_check] is operations control and live machine control remain absent

  = must: require completion review before any implementation output is accepted
  = must: fail implementation review if any proof check fails

